{"term":"Latin","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:55f3cc054f4f8b7e12","definition":"Of or relating to Latin: the language spoken in ancient Rome and other cities of Latium.","example":"Africa was the natural leader because there the number of Christians who were of Roman origin and Latin speech was probably far greater than in so cosmopolitan a city as Rome.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable","register":"not-comparable","wordFamily":["Latin-1","Latin alphabet","Latin America","Latin cross","Latin grammar school","Latin hip-hop","Latin Quarter","Latin school","Latin script","Latin square","Latin time","Traditional Latin Mass","Vulgar Latin"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Latin#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0b66ce05c3c96370b6","definition":"Of or relating to the script of the language spoken in ancient Rome and many modern alphabets.","example":"The Serbo-Croatian incunabula printed in Latin letters are indubitably the products of a very modest establishment.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["Roman"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable","register":"not-comparable","wordFamily":["Latin-1","Latin alphabet","Latin America","Latin cross","Latin grammar school","Latin hip-hop","Latin Quarter","Latin school","Latin script","Latin square","Latin time","Traditional Latin Mass","Vulgar Latin"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Latin#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:320cedd48fced05394","definition":"Of or relating to ancient Rome or its Empire.","example":"The earliest Latin culture of Ireland was heavily indebted to that of Britain[…]","pos":"adj","synonyms":["Roman"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable","register":"not-comparable","wordFamily":["Latin-1","Latin alphabet","Latin America","Latin cross","Latin grammar school","Latin hip-hop","Latin Quarter","Latin school","Latin script","Latin square","Latin time","Traditional Latin Mass","Vulgar Latin"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Latin#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:01b15b2b4c8c199856","definition":"Of or relating to Latium (modern Lazio), the region around Rome.","example":"From the Campagna and the Latin hills, the flame of rebellion spread to Antium and Terracina, and to the most remote allies of the Romans, the cities of the Campanian plains.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["Latian"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable","register":"not-comparable","wordFamily":["Latin-1","Latin alphabet","Latin America","Latin cross","Latin grammar school","Latin hip-hop","Latin Quarter","Latin school","Latin script","Latin square","Latin time","Traditional Latin Mass","Vulgar Latin"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Latin#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3352da5928748d3653","definition":"Of or relating to the customs and people descended from the ancient Romans and their Empire.","example":"Major for joy, Minor for sadness, is apparently a significance which the German nations read into these scales; while the Semitic, Latin, and Slavic nations do not share this conception.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["Romance"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable","register":"not-comparable","wordFamily":["Latin-1","Latin alphabet","Latin America","Latin cross","Latin grammar school","Latin hip-hop","Latin Quarter","Latin school","Latin script","Latin square","Latin time","Traditional Latin Mass","Vulgar Latin"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Latin#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5e142147db10f03408","definition":"Of or from Latin America or of Latin American culture.","example":"As such, today's Latin music is a synthesis of European, African, and the few indigenous elements that remain.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["Latin American","Latino"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable","register":"not-comparable","wordFamily":["Latin-1","Latin alphabet","Latin America","Latin cross","Latin grammar school","Latin hip-hop","Latin Quarter","Latin school","Latin script","Latin square","Latin time","Traditional Latin Mass","Vulgar Latin"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Latin#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3206b040f413dac6ed","definition":"Roman Catholic; of or pertaining to the Roman Rite of the Catholic Church.","example":"The Latin bishop now took the Greek bishop by the hand and conducted him to his throne[…]","pos":"adj","synonyms":["Catholic","Roman","Roman Catholic"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable","register":"not-comparable","wordFamily":["Latin-1","Latin alphabet","Latin America","Latin cross","Latin grammar school","Latin hip-hop","Latin Quarter","Latin school","Latin script","Latin square","Latin time","Traditional Latin Mass","Vulgar Latin"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Latin#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:1b5737d10de08868c9","definition":"The language of the ancient Romans, other Latins and of the Roman Catholic church, especially Classical Latin.","example":"Supper being over, the lawyer took his leave, and the doctor began to ſound the learned clerk reſpecting his proficiency in the dead languages. \"As to dead languages,\" replied the ſchoolmafter, \"I was once a vaſt pretty ſcholar indeed, but want of exercise has made me main ſlack—I can't get over my ground as I uſed to do. Then as to the t'other dead fellow, I could never greek it at all, that's flat. And, Lord bleſs you! my Latin is of no more uſe to me here than—than—\" Here he ſtuck for want of a ſimile; when Mr. Le Dupe helped him out by ſaying, \"that it is to a young man at college, where it is conſidered a pedantic inſult, and an unpardonable bore, to utter a Latin ſentence.\"","pos":"name","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"uncountable","wordFamily":["Latin-1","Latin alphabet","Latin America","Latin cross","Latin grammar school","Latin hip-hop","Latin Quarter","Latin school","Latin script","Latin square","Latin time","Traditional Latin Mass","Vulgar Latin"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Latin#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ebaa847595b82efdf6","definition":"The Latin alphabet or writing system.","example":"","pos":"name","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["Latin-1","Latin alphabet","Latin America","Latin cross","Latin grammar school","Latin hip-hop","Latin Quarter","Latin school","Latin script","Latin square","Latin time","Traditional Latin Mass","Vulgar Latin"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Latin#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:26af47a01e5fee01e8","definition":"The nonsense placeholder text (often based on real Latin) used in greeking.","example":"","pos":"name","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["Latin-1","Latin alphabet","Latin America","Latin cross","Latin grammar school","Latin hip-hop","Latin Quarter","Latin school","Latin script","Latin square","Latin time","T