ns.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["Latin-1","Latin alphabet","Latin America","Latin cross","Latin grammar school","Latin hip-hop","Latin Quarter","Latin school","Latin script","Latin square","Latin time","Traditional Latin Mass","Vulgar Latin"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Latin#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:1016c6b2ad464c2a8e","definition":"A person from Latin America.","example":"In the use of patent medicine the average Latin resembles the American of fifty years ago, who generally had a bottle of some concoction on which he depended whenever he felt out of sorts.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["Latin American","Latino"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["Latin-1","Latin alphabet","Latin America","Latin cross","Latin grammar school","Latin hip-hop","Latin Quarter","Latin school","Latin script","Latin square","Latin time","Traditional Latin Mass","Vulgar Latin"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Latin#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:14b5e05ee258bbbdfa","definition":"A person adhering to Roman Catholic practice.","example":"The modern Latins have been in the habit of blaming the Greek and other Eastern Liturgies for not consecrating by the recital of OUR SAVIOUR'S words of Institution[…]","pos":"noun","synonyms":["Catholic","Roman","Roman Catholic"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["Latin-1","Latin alphabet","Latin America","Latin cross","Latin grammar school","Latin hip-hop","Latin Quarter","Latin school","Latin script","Latin square","Latin time","Traditional Latin Mass","Vulgar Latin"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourc